# Dev-server-only knobs. Expo CLI loads this next to `.env` whenever
# NODE_ENV=development (`expo start`, `expo run:android|ios`). Nothing here is
# EXPO_PUBLIC_*, so nothing is inlined into the app bundle.
#
# Lazy bundling makes every `import()` in the app a Metro split point, and Metro
# builds and retains a SEPARATE server-side module graph per split entry. In
# this app any such graph is ~7.5k modules (~500 MB of heap) because the import
# graph is dense, so two or three `import()`s hit in one session push the dev
# server past Node's 2 GB default heap:
#   FATAL ERROR: Reached heap limit Allocation failed - JavaScript heap out of memory
# It trims fewer than 1% of modules from the initial bundle (8,953 vs 9,028), so
# it buys nothing here. Measured 2026-09-20; see CLAUDE.md "Metro lazy bundling".
EXPO_NO_METRO_LAZY=1
